s += [
step('disc-sprocket-off','Expose both sides of the hub','Record the installed disc and sprocket faces/orientations before removal. Support the wheel without loading the disc. Remove the six sprocket self-locking nuts and retain the bolt/washer arrangement by location; remove the sprocket. Remove the six brake-disc bolts and lift off the disc. Keep friction surfaces clear of grease and locking agent.',[135,136,137],'Sprocket/disc orientation and hardware recorded; hub accessible; disc protected.',True),
step('seals-clip-out','Remove seals and bearing retention','Clean the hub exterior. Lever out both old oil seals with a flat-head screwdriver, using a cloth between tool and wheel to protect the hub. Remove the right-side bearing circlip with suitable circlip pliers before attempting to extract that bearing. Retain old seals and clip only for matching replacements.',[131,135],'Both seals and right-side circlip removed; bearing retention released.'),
step('bearings-out','Extract all three old bearings','Use an appropriate bearing puller as Yamaha specifies. Remove the single right-side bearing and retain the internal spacer; extract both left-side bearings. Keep their side/order identified against PDF135/137. Support the hub for the puller reaction; do not force a bearing against retained hardware or damage its housing.',[131,135,137],'Three old bearings removed: right one, left two; internal spacer retained.'),
step('hub-inspection','Inspect the hub and spacer','Clean and inspect bearing seats, circlip groove, internal spacer and external collars for damage or wear. Record whether the original hub and spacer remain serviceable. Check axle bending on a flat surface; do not straighten it. Check tire/wheel condition now; measure runout after the wheel is refitted on its axle as instructed in the final check. A damaged seat, spacer, axle, disc or worn sprocket requires its own repair/replacement decision; this guide does not authorize machining or truing.',[131,136],'Hub/spacer/collars and axle condition recorded; no unresolved damage accepted; runout deferred until axle refit.',True),
step('right-bearing','Fit the right bearing first','Identify the brake-disc/right side and the single matching new bearing. Install it first into its original seat, pressing the outer race square and parallel with a correctly sized driver/socket. Follow the PDF137 arrangement and general marked-face-outward orientation. Do not drive through the inner race or use compressed air to spin the bearing.',[25,135,137],'Right-side new bearing square in its original seat; correct side and marked-face orientation checked.'),
step('new-circlip','Fit new right-side retention','Install the matching new circlip into the right-side hub groove. Follow the general PDF25 edge/force orientation and exact PDF135/137 retaining position; do not overexpand it. Verify the full circumference is seated in the groove before covering it with the seal. If bearing position prevents seating, correct the assembly rather than forcing the clip.',[25,135,137],'New circlip fully seated; bearing retained; edge orientation checked.',True),
step('spacer-left-bearings','Restore the spacer and both left bearings','Insert the original serviceable internal spacer in the PDF137 position between the right bearing and left bearing pair. Fit both matching new left-side bearings in the order/positions shown in PDF135/137. Press each outer race square and parallel with a matching driver. Keep the spacer correctly located; do not omit it or force a cocked bearing. Verify the stack and smooth bearing rotation before installing seals.',[25,135,137],'Internal spacer present; two left bearings installed; all three bearings turn smoothly and stack matches drawing.',True),
step('new-seals','Install both new wheel seals','Apply lithium-soap-based grease to both new seal lips. Face their manufacturer marks/numbers outward and the main lips toward the hub interior. Drive each seal evenly using a socket/driver matching its outside diameter. Set both at the approximate1.0 mm recess shown by dimension a in the two PDF135 cross-sections; do not copy the front-wheel flush setting. Measure and record each recess against the illustrated hub-face reference.',[25,135,137],'Both new seals oriented and undamaged; left/right approximate1.0 mm recess recorded.',True),
step('sprocket-refit','Refit the original serviceable sprocket','Clean the hub/sprocket mating faces and restore the recorded original orientation and bolt/washer arrangement. This workflow uses matching new self-locking nuts. Tighten all six nuts progressively in a crisscross pattern to42 N·m. Inspect that the sprocket sits fully against the hub. Worn or bent teeth require matched drive/rear sprocket replacement outside this retained-sprocket operation.',[135,136,137],'Six sprocket nuts42 N·m in staged crisscross pattern; mating faces seated.',True),
step('disc-refit','Refit the original serviceable disc','Restore the recorded disc orientation against clean mating faces. Apply the specified LOCTITE locking agent at the disc-bolt threads and tighten all six bolts progressively in a crisscross pattern to12 N·m. The OEM source does not identify a grade or cure time here; record the actual product and follow its instructions. Keep grease/locking agent away from friction faces and inspect seating.',[135,137],'Six disc bolts12 N·m in stages/crisscross; actual locking agent recorded; disc seated and friction faces clean.',True),
]
